# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify static rewrites (WS-5.7).
# The canonical share link is  https://<domain>/import?n=&d=  but a static host
# has no /import file, so it 404s without a rewrite. A 200 rewrite serves
# index.html WHILE preserving the query string (the n=&d= payload the landing's
# deferred-install redirector reads). NOT a 30x redirect — a redirect to "/"
# would still work via the landing's /?n=&d= fallback, but the rewrite keeps the
# clean /import path that assetlinks.json / apple-app-site-association point at.
#
# Host setup TODO (Vasily, once the owned domain + Cloudflare Pages exist):
#   - drop this file at the site root (Cloudflare Pages reads /_redirects automatically)
#   - Netlify uses the same syntax; Vercel needs an equivalent rule in vercel.json
#   - the landing ALSO handles /?n=&d= so the loop degrades gracefully if rewrites are missing

/import      /index.html   200
/import/*    /index.html   200
/a/*         /index.html   200
